SCHEMA TYPE options:
we can declare the type using the schema directly

Schema validation with update:runValidators: true is an option used to enforce schema validation during update queries. By default, Mongoose automatically runs validators when you use .save() or .create(), but skips them during update operations like updateOne(), updateMany(), or findOneAndUpdate()
Passing { runValidators: true } ensures that any new data being sent to the database conforms to your schema definitions

